WEBVTT

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:06.840
Two make-good prices can look very
different because they cover different

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.900
work. Start with the lease and condition
records.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.860
Ask your solicitor to clarify the
obligation, then have the right appointed

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.580
specialists assess the physical scope.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:20.260
When proposals arrive, check the same
items: what stays, what is removed,

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:25.860
services interfaces, access, disposal,
allowances and the GST basis.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:30.260
A rate per square metre is not a verified
quote for your premises.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:34.740
An itemised brief helps you see what is
included and what is still uncertain.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:39.580
Plan the handback evidence as well: scope
revisions, relevant photos, required

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:41.920
records and an owner for each outstanding
action.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:46.540
Returning keys and obtaining a legal
release are different matters, so confirm

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:48.240
the actual requirements with your
solicitor.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:52.260
Our free make-good worksheet helps
organise the questions.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:57.100
Read the guide and discuss the client-side
coordination scope with YOS if you

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:58.100
need support.
